#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0410 expect=noViolation domain=SV
#note "Authority: SDTM/SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0410, Condition 'Scheduled or Contingent visit (exists in TV)', Rule 'VISITNUM identifies unique record within subject'. Every planned VISITNUM (1, 2, 3 -- all in TV) occurs once per subject; subject S1-002 reuses 1 and 2, which is fine because uniqueness is WITHIN subject. Row 3 is an unplanned visit numbered 1.5 (non-integral, not in TV), recorded once -> outside the Condition. No row the authority flags -> silent. VISITNUM is Num on both sides."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVSTDTC  type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Visit"
---
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1   | SCREENING       | 2024-01-02
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 2   | BASELINE        | 2024-01-10
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 1.5 | UNSCHEDULED 1.5 | 2024-01-06
S1 | SV | S1-001 | 3   | WEEK 4          | 2024-02-07
S1 | SV | S1-002 | 1   | SCREENING       | 2024-01-03
S1 | SV | S1-002 | 2   | BASELINE        | 2024-01-11
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col TVSTRL   type=Char label="Visit Start Rule"
---
S1 | TV | 1 | SCREENING | Start of screening
S1 | TV | 2 | BASELINE  | Day 1
S1 | TV | 3 | WEEK 4    | Day 29
---
